1
00:00:00,097 --> 00:00:01,833
A million people's salaries.

2
00:00:02,264 --> 00:00:05,847
Ninety-nine megabytes — twenty-six million tokens.

3
00:00:06,278 --> 00:00:08,194
No AI can read a file this size.

4
00:00:08,653 --> 00:00:11,069
And you would never paste it into one anyway.

5
00:00:11,579 --> 00:00:13,657
So watch one analyse it anyway,

6
00:00:14,133 --> 00:00:16,443
without ever seeing a single row.

7
00:00:16,933 --> 00:00:19,765
Every column is graded before the agent is told

8
00:00:19,765 --> 00:00:20,951
the file exists.

9
00:00:21,347 --> 00:00:23,974
Name, email, employee ID — sealed.

10
00:00:24,370 --> 00:00:25,530
It cannot group by them,

11
00:00:25,938 --> 00:00:28,158
filter on them, or ever receive them.

12
00:00:28,658 --> 00:00:32,044
The grading is a heuristic — column names and how

13
00:00:32,044 --> 00:00:35,260
unique the values are — so sometimes it will be

14
00:00:35,260 --> 00:00:35,585
wrong.

15
00:00:36,002 --> 00:00:37,031
One click overrules it.

16
00:00:37,460 --> 00:00:39,244
Watch what happens when I seal a column the

17
00:00:39,244 --> 00:00:43,124
agent was just using: every tool is withdrawn and

18
00:00:43,124 --> 00:00:46,913
re-registered, the descriptions rewritten around the new grading,

19
00:00:47,330 --> 00:00:49,062
and the query that worked a moment ago is

20
00:00:49,075 --> 00:00:49,830
refused.

21
00:00:50,350 --> 00:00:53,488
Eight WebMCP tools, and notice what is missing:

22
00:00:53,960 --> 00:00:55,580
there is no run_sql.

23
00:00:55,988 --> 00:00:58,284
The agent cannot write a query at all.

24
00:00:58,705 --> 00:00:59,738
It fills in a form,

25
00:01:00,031 --> 00:01:01,243
and the page compiles it.

26
00:01:01,677 --> 00:01:04,712
The same eight tools appear in ChatGPT and in

27
00:01:04,712 --> 00:01:05,899
Chrome behind the flag.

28
00:01:06,294 --> 00:01:08,156
This is the standard, not one app.

29
00:01:08,662 --> 00:01:09,170
Schema.

30
00:01:09,587 --> 00:01:10,589
Cohort comparison.

31
00:01:11,019 --> 00:01:11,410
Chart.

32
00:01:11,826 --> 00:01:15,003
Each one across all one million rows in under

33
00:01:15,016 --> 00:01:15,954
a tenth of a second.

34
00:01:16,370 --> 00:01:17,959
And look at what just happened with that chart:

35
00:01:18,350 --> 00:01:19,522
the agent asked for it,

36
00:01:19,756 --> 00:01:21,891
I can see it, and the agent got back

37
00:01:21,904 --> 00:01:22,894
one word — drawn.

38
00:01:23,363 --> 00:01:25,368
Three percent pay gap at the junior levels,

39
00:01:25,615 --> 00:01:27,477
thirteen at the senior ones.

40
00:01:27,991 --> 00:01:29,293
Ask who is paid most,

41
00:01:29,684 --> 00:01:30,726
and it refuses.

42
00:01:31,142 --> 00:01:33,720
A maximum is one real person's salary.

43
00:01:34,150 --> 00:01:36,559
And the refusal tells the agent what to ask

44
00:01:36,559 --> 00:01:39,033
instead, so it recovers on the next turn.

45
00:01:39,548 --> 00:01:42,567
But a counter reading zero is just this page

46
00:01:42,580 --> 00:01:44,229
marking its own homework.

47
00:01:44,655 --> 00:01:47,341
So the page revokes its own network access.

48
00:01:47,766 --> 00:01:50,413
Watch me try to leak the data on purpose.

49
00:01:50,931 --> 00:01:51,317
Fetch.

50
00:01:51,729 --> 00:01:52,434
XHR.

51
00:01:52,673 --> 00:01:53,524
WebSocket.

52
00:01:53,977 --> 00:01:54,309
Beacon.

53
00:01:54,735 --> 00:01:55,719
Tracking pixel.

54
00:01:56,131 --> 00:01:57,793
Chrome refuses all five.

55
00:01:58,313 --> 00:02:01,221
And this is every byte the agent actually received.

56
00:02:01,655 --> 00:02:03,668
Not a summary — the literal text.

57
00:02:04,090 --> 00:02:05,037
Search it for a name,

58
00:02:05,432 --> 00:02:06,248
and there is none.

59
00:02:06,764 --> 00:02:08,316
Ninety-nine megabytes in.

60
00:02:08,769 --> 00:02:09,594
Kilobytes out.

61
00:02:10,047 --> 00:02:10,981
Zero rows.

62
00:02:11,420 --> 00:02:13,907
And it holds: ten million rows,

63
00:02:14,127 --> 00:02:18,069
a full gigabyte, every query still under a second.

64
00:02:18,536 --> 00:02:22,107
Blindfold — analyse a file your AI could never read.
